# RTKDirect contribution — chained off the local UFO1 mount.
#
# Why chained rather than a second -out on @ufo1: str2str accepts at most THREE
# output streams and a fourth SEGVs (no bounds check in RTKLIB).  @ufo1 already
# uses its three.  Chaining is also what the local ntripc mount on :2104 exists
# for -- it is the fan-out point, and until now nothing consumed it.
#
# Cost of the chain: one extra hop of latency (sub-millisecond on loopback) and
# a dependency -- if @ufo1 stops, this stops receiving.  Both acceptable; the
# alternative is a second full transcode of the same SBF.
#
# Shell-sourced by str2str-relay-exec, so ARGS is quoted; see instances/ssr.env.
IN=ntrip://127.0.0.1:2104/UFO1_MSM7
ARGS="-r 10000"
# Input is already RTCM3, so no conversion: PUSH_FMT must be empty.
PUSH_FMT=""
PUSH_CREDS="RTKDIRECT"
RTKDIRECT_HOST=ntrip.rtkdirect.com:2101
